what = IntroWhat(
  "Trainees often aren't allowed to touch the real software: they lack the role, it holds real people's data, or one wrong click sends real money. This topic covers why we simulate, the five ways to build a simulation and the tools for each, how to keep it matching the real software release after release (including as code and with AI), and the principles that make a simulation actually teach.",
  "An interactive user manual is a simulation of a software system that lets people practise real tasks (clicking, typing, making mistakes) without using the live system.",
  [
    "Why simulate: least privilege, production data, irreversible actions and licence cost",
    "Five approaches, from screenshot guides to hotspot simulations, DOM capture, UI clones and training sandboxes, and their tools",
    "Maintainability: upkeep cost, drift detection, version labels, and what can be done as code or with AI",
    "Creation principles: task-first, selective fidelity, safe to fail, and Watch → Try → Test",
  ],
  ["documentation", "training", "simulation", "software-adoption", "maintainability"],
)

why = IntroWhy(
  "A manual people can practise in beats a manual people read, but only while it still matches the real software.",
  "Teams that pick an approach without thinking about upkeep end up with the Drifted Phantom UI: a simulation of screens that no longer exist, which trains people to do the wrong thing with confidence.",
)
